 **Steps:**
-1. Compute the absolute value of the normal components: $a = |n|$.
-2. Apply the hardness parameter $k$ to the absolute normal components: $w = a^k$.
-3. Normalize the weights to sum to 1.0: $W = w / (w_x + w_y + w_z)$.
-4. Sample the texture for each of the three planes using the position components as UV coordinates:
-   - XY plane (weighted by Z): $c_{xy} = \text{sample}(tex, p_{xy})$
-   - XZ plane (weighted by Y): $c_{xz} = \text{sample}(tex, p_{xz})$
-   - YZ plane (weighted by X): $c_{yz} = \text{sample}(tex, p_{yz})$
