 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Zero Normal:** If the normal is zero, the weights are undefined. Guard against this by ensuring the normal is normalized before use.
-- **Degenerate Normals:** If two components of the normal are zero (e.g., along an axis), the division by sum of weights is still valid as long as at least one component is non-zero.
